       "en": "No *don’t* when the sentence has **am / is / are** or **can / will / should**: just add **not** after that word. **I’m not tired.** **It isn’t far** (or *It’s not far*). **I can’t swim.** **I won’t tell** (*won’t* = will not). Never “I don’t am” or “I don’t can”.",
       "fr": "Pas de *don’t* quand la phrase a **am / is / are** ou **can / will / should** : on ajoute juste **not** après ce mot. **I’m not tired.** **It isn’t far** (ou *It’s not far*). **I can’t swim.** **I won’t tell** (*won’t* = will not). Jamais « I don’t am » ni « I don’t can ».",
