       "en": "« Plus grand **que** » → **bigger than**. Short words (one beat, or two beats ending in *-y*) add **-er**: **cheaper**, **bigger**, **hotter**, **busier**. Long words use **more**: **more expensive**, **more comfortable**, **more beautiful**. Then **than** (= que): **Tampa is hotter than Paris.** Never “more big”, and never “bigger that”.",
       "fr": "« Plus grand **que** » → **bigger than**. Les mots courts (une syllabe, ou deux qui finissent par *-y*) prennent **-er** : **cheaper**, **bigger**, **hotter**, **busier**. Les mots longs prennent **more** : **more expensive**, **more comfortable**, **more beautiful**. Puis **than** (= que) : **Tampa is hotter than Paris.** Jamais « more big », et jamais « bigger that ».",
