       "en": "For more than one, most words just add **-s**: *one client, two clients*. But some of the most common words change completely: one person → two **people**; one child → two **children**; one man → two **men**; one woman → two **women**; one tooth → two **teeth**; one foot → two **feet**; one mouse → two **mice**. These never take *-s*: no “peoples”, “childrens” or “tooths”.",
